WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.923
- Hi, I'm Steven,

00:00:00.923 --> 00:00:02.027
and I recently made a video

00:00:02.027 --> 00:00:04.298
where I train with a
K-pop star for one week.

00:00:04.298 --> 00:00:06.432
In that video, an actual
K-pop star, Amber Liu,

00:00:06.432 --> 00:00:07.829
sent me advice from Korea,

00:00:07.829 --> 00:00:10.093
and today, I finally
get to meet my sensei.

00:00:10.093 --> 00:00:10.926
We're gonna hang out.

00:00:10.926 --> 00:00:11.759
We're gonna eat some good food,

00:00:11.759 --> 00:00:13.036
and see what a day in a life

00:00:13.036 --> 00:00:14.792
of a K-pop star really is.

00:00:14.792 --> 00:00:15.682
Let's go.

00:00:15.682 --> 00:00:19.849
(Screaming and applause)
(creaking)

00:00:21.482 --> 00:00:24.065
(upbeat music)

00:00:25.927 --> 00:00:26.864
Welcome to Buzzfeed.

00:00:26.864 --> 00:00:27.715
- Thank you.

00:00:27.715 --> 00:00:28.548
- So, what are you doing in LA right now?

00:00:28.548 --> 00:00:29.381
- I came to see you.

00:00:29.381 --> 00:00:30.214
- Oh.

00:00:30.214 --> 00:00:31.047
- And, to eat tacos.

00:00:31.047 --> 00:00:31.880
- That's it?

00:00:31.880 --> 00:00:32.713
- Yes.

00:00:32.713 --> 00:00:33.546
I'm actually here for KCON.

00:00:33.546 --> 00:00:34.379
Been going every year.

00:00:34.379 --> 00:00:35.610
Artist's come from Korea to perform.

00:00:35.610 --> 00:00:36.520
All around the world,

00:00:36.520 --> 00:00:38.884
like France, Dubai, New York.

00:00:38.884 --> 00:00:39.717
- You were in France?

00:00:39.717 --> 00:00:40.550
- I was in France.

00:00:40.550 --> 00:00:41.811
I'm going global.
[Steven] You've got the life.

00:00:41.811 --> 00:00:42.644
- Yeah, international, baby.

00:00:42.644 --> 00:00:43.502
(claps) Mm.

00:00:43.502 --> 00:00:44.335
On the side,

00:00:44.335 --> 00:00:46.633
I'm shooting a show called Ranting Monkey

00:00:46.633 --> 00:00:47.466
- [Steven] So you have your own show.

00:00:47.466 --> 00:00:48.299
- [Amber] Yeah, my own show.

00:00:48.299 --> 00:00:49.132
- [Steven] That's dedicated to you.

00:00:49.132 --> 00:00:50.186
- [Amber] Because I'm fabulous.

00:00:50.186 --> 00:00:51.449
- I actually asked my Twitter followers

00:00:51.449 --> 00:00:53.278
what they want to ask K-pop stars,

00:00:53.278 --> 00:00:54.256
like are you getting enough rest?

00:00:54.256 --> 00:00:56.762
- Because I'm so passionate,
and I love what I do,

00:00:56.762 --> 00:00:58.525
I don't think about sleep,
I don't think about eating,

00:00:58.525 --> 00:01:00.466
my team, they tell me "Amber eat",

00:01:00.466 --> 00:01:02.539
I'm like oh, okay.

00:01:02.539 --> 00:01:03.372
- What's your favorite food,

00:01:03.372 --> 00:01:04.317
let's go get your favorite food.

00:01:04.317 --> 00:01:05.920
- Can we just get Jack-n-the-Box tacos,

00:01:05.920 --> 00:01:07.758
I really like Jack in the Box tacos.

00:01:07.758 --> 00:01:08.700
Dude, two for a dollar man.

00:01:08.700 --> 00:01:10.443
- Two for a dollar, you're a K-pop star!

00:01:10.443 --> 00:01:12.416
- It's a great deal, get 20 tacos,

00:01:12.416 --> 00:01:15.115
get a bag full of taco sauce.

00:01:15.115 --> 00:01:16.245
- Let's do it, alright let's go.

00:01:16.245 --> 00:01:17.124
Let's get out of here.

00:01:17.124 --> 00:01:17.957
- Out!

00:01:17.957 --> 00:01:19.941
So like, apart from my K-pop life,

00:01:19.941 --> 00:01:23.094
I use to work at my friend's taco shop.

00:01:23.094 --> 00:01:23.927
- What, when?

00:01:23.927 --> 00:01:26.453
- I actually can't cook, so
I can't fry an egg properly,

00:01:26.453 --> 00:01:27.923
so I went in everyday.

00:01:27.923 --> 00:01:29.595
- [Steven] To?
- [Amber] To work.

00:01:29.595 --> 00:01:30.892
- [Steven] Wow.
- [Amber] And make tacos.

00:01:30.892 --> 00:01:34.868
I really missed out living the
quote in quote normal life.

00:01:34.868 --> 00:01:36.547
- [Steven] Yeah, you're
elevated in society.

00:01:36.547 --> 00:01:39.064
- So I try to surround
myself in an environment

00:01:39.064 --> 00:01:40.328
where I don't have those privileges,

00:01:40.328 --> 00:01:43.854
because everything that
I do is a blessing.

00:01:43.854 --> 00:01:45.780
You know, I sing and dance for a living.

00:01:45.780 --> 00:01:49.521
There's so much more to this
life than just my world.

00:01:49.521 --> 00:01:50.354
- Yeah.

00:01:53.854 --> 00:01:55.431
I can't believe I'm at
Jack in the Box right now.

00:01:55.431 --> 00:01:58.046
- I want to, can we like 10 of these.

00:01:58.046 --> 00:02:01.059
- Can we get like 20 monster tacos please?

00:02:01.059 --> 00:02:02.963
We went all out, go big or go home.

00:02:02.963 --> 00:02:05.546
(upbeat music)

00:02:08.189 --> 00:02:09.440
You have an crazy fan stories?

00:02:09.440 --> 00:02:12.366
- I don't have those crazy
fans that people talk about.

00:02:12.366 --> 00:02:14.001
They're called sasaeng type fans.

00:02:14.001 --> 00:02:15.127
Sasaeng is like your private life.

00:02:15.127 --> 00:02:16.671
- [Steven] Oh.

00:02:16.671 --> 00:02:18.952
- I don't control sasaeng fans fans,

00:02:18.952 --> 00:02:20.381
because they are stalking you.

00:02:20.381 --> 00:02:21.616
I have a lot of other
celebrity friends who have

00:02:21.616 --> 00:02:24.198
sasaeng fans, I do not
know how they function.

00:02:24.198 --> 00:02:26.948
As a friend, I want the best
for whoever I like, right?

00:02:26.948 --> 00:02:29.450
Say, like if I have a
dating scandal or whatever

00:02:29.450 --> 00:02:31.402
with somebody, and they
hate on my boyfriend.

00:02:31.402 --> 00:02:33.346
- Not me, don't hate on me.

00:02:33.346 --> 00:02:34.372
- Respect their private life.

00:02:34.372 --> 00:02:35.318
- You have good fans.

00:02:35.318 --> 00:02:37.121
- My fans are the best,
I'm so proud of you.

00:02:37.121 --> 00:02:39.371
(cheering)

00:02:41.835 --> 00:02:42.915
- I want you to meet a friend of mine.

00:02:42.915 --> 00:02:43.882
- Okay.
- Her name is Jen.

00:02:43.882 --> 00:02:44.715
- Okay.

00:02:44.715 --> 00:02:45.994
- They say she is the Amber of Buzzfeed.

00:02:45.994 --> 00:02:46.827
- Ooh.

00:02:46.827 --> 00:02:48.161
- And most importantly, she's a tomboy.

00:02:48.161 --> 00:02:49.119
- Ooh, I love tomboys.

00:02:49.119 --> 00:02:50.952
She must be very sexy.

00:02:52.704 --> 00:02:53.537
- Hi!

00:02:53.537 --> 00:02:54.660
- Oh my God, I know who you are!

00:02:54.660 --> 00:02:56.467
I really like her, she's cool!

00:02:56.467 --> 00:02:57.300
- Come here!

00:02:57.300 --> 00:02:59.090
Nice to meet you!

00:02:59.090 --> 00:03:00.202
- Come on over!

00:03:00.202 --> 00:03:01.201
- I see you on the internet!

00:03:01.201 --> 00:03:02.217
- Jen's my best friend here at Buzzfeed,

00:03:02.217 --> 00:03:03.575
and we just wanted to talk to you,

00:03:03.575 --> 00:03:05.432
but first we have a present for you.

00:03:05.432 --> 00:03:07.907
(Amber squeals)
- Hot cheetos!

00:03:07.907 --> 00:03:09.030
- Do you like hot cheetos?

00:03:09.030 --> 00:03:09.892
- I love hot cheetos.

00:03:09.892 --> 00:03:11.734
- Dude I eat hot cheetos every morning.

00:03:11.734 --> 00:03:12.987
- I'm very happy right now.

00:03:12.987 --> 00:03:15.834
- I gave y'all these snacks
because I want to talk about,

00:03:15.834 --> 00:03:17.943
about you more so now.

00:03:17.943 --> 00:03:18.955
We don't want to hear about K-pop.

00:03:18.955 --> 00:03:21.030
You're famous, whatever,
like yeah that's cool.

00:03:21.030 --> 00:03:22.498
You guys are beautiful women.

00:03:22.498 --> 00:03:23.715
- [Jen And Amber] Thank you.

00:03:23.715 --> 00:03:26.031
- And you guys also don't
dress as what people

00:03:26.031 --> 00:03:28.536
traditionally think as
female, like historically.

00:03:28.536 --> 00:03:30.129
Can you tell me a little about that?

00:03:30.129 --> 00:03:32.898
- I have a big phobia of public bathrooms.

00:03:32.898 --> 00:03:35.185
I've been harassed a lot,
like verbally harassed.

00:03:35.185 --> 00:03:36.936
Someone would be like
"Oh, girls bathroom."

00:03:36.936 --> 00:03:38.035
like "Oh, I am a girl."

00:03:38.035 --> 00:03:39.151
They could just leave
it at that, that's fine.

00:03:39.151 --> 00:03:41.169
You don't look like a girl, (mumbling).

00:03:41.169 --> 00:03:42.268
Like, how dare you come into the bathroom,

00:03:42.268 --> 00:03:43.532
and then I don't believe you!

00:03:43.532 --> 00:03:44.365
- Oh my God.

00:03:44.365 --> 00:03:46.532
- I don't blame people
for being surprised,

00:03:46.532 --> 00:03:50.199
I just don't know what to
do when they over react.

00:03:50.199 --> 00:03:51.816
Do you want me to show you?

00:03:51.816 --> 00:03:53.335
(giggling)

00:03:53.335 --> 00:03:55.012
I don't know what else to do.

00:03:55.012 --> 00:03:56.216
Just because I dress a certain way,

00:03:56.216 --> 00:03:58.961
they think "Oh Amber
wants to become a boy."

00:03:58.961 --> 00:04:01.078
I just like comfortable
clothing, I like sports,

00:04:01.078 --> 00:04:02.647
and I just happen to have short hair.

00:04:02.647 --> 00:04:05.079
- Everybody's sort of held to
a certain gender expectations,

00:04:05.079 --> 00:04:07.088
and I think if you
deviate outside of that,

00:04:07.088 --> 00:04:09.071
people don't know how to respond.

00:04:09.071 --> 00:04:10.774
- Even for guys, like be a man.

00:04:10.774 --> 00:04:11.946
That just sounds very pressuring.

00:04:11.946 --> 00:04:14.837
We should respect the person
for their individualness

00:04:14.837 --> 00:04:16.460
rather than okay, just
because you're this,

00:04:16.460 --> 00:04:17.567
you're just mph.

00:04:17.567 --> 00:04:20.265
- Be yourself.
- Be myself.

00:04:20.265 --> 00:04:21.748
- Yo, what are you playing?

00:04:21.748 --> 00:04:22.681
- Pokemon Go.

00:04:22.681 --> 00:04:24.241
- Did you play Pokemon
when you were younger?

00:04:24.241 --> 00:04:25.775
- Yes, I have all the cards.

00:04:25.775 --> 00:04:27.062
- Oh my gosh, I played--

00:04:27.062 --> 00:04:29.229
- Wait, quite quite quite.

00:04:30.172 --> 00:04:32.271
- If you think you're that
much of a Pokemon fan girl,

00:04:32.271 --> 00:04:34.936
we're going to play a
spelling bee of Pokemon.

00:04:34.936 --> 00:04:37.929
- Exeggcute.
- Oh my God, EGGE--

00:04:37.929 --> 00:04:39.601
- [Steven] Wrong!
- What? What the hell?

00:04:39.601 --> 00:04:41.253
- Aerodactyl.
- AR--

00:04:41.253 --> 00:04:42.586
- Nope.
- AY--

00:04:42.586 --> 00:04:44.467
- Nope. Kangaskhan.

00:04:44.467 --> 00:04:47.967
- Oh my gosh. KANGASKHAN.

00:04:51.695 --> 00:04:54.278
- Woah!
- [Amber] Kangaskhan.

00:04:54.278 --> 00:04:55.793
- [Steven] Kangaskhan.

00:04:55.793 --> 00:04:58.446
(upbeat music)

00:04:58.446 --> 00:04:59.487
We're here at some random skate park.

00:04:59.487 --> 00:05:00.320
- [Amber] Yes.

00:05:00.320 --> 00:05:01.345
- Amber said she's gonna skate.

00:05:01.345 --> 00:05:02.178
- Yes.

00:05:02.178 --> 00:05:03.436
- Cause I've never done this before.

00:05:03.436 --> 00:05:06.019
(guitar music)

00:05:08.024 --> 00:05:10.445
You actually live like a
pretty, not like a normal life,

00:05:10.445 --> 00:05:13.951
but you do enjoy a lot of
the things that people do.

00:05:13.951 --> 00:05:15.514
- There's so much cool stuff in the world,

00:05:15.514 --> 00:05:17.511
I just want to experience
as much as I can before.

00:05:17.511 --> 00:05:20.704
(guitar music)

00:05:20.704 --> 00:05:23.437
Skateboarding is all about
overcoming your fears.

00:05:23.437 --> 00:05:24.687
- [Steven] Huh.

00:05:29.146 --> 00:05:31.958
- Whether it's skating,
eating tacos, going on stage,

00:05:31.958 --> 00:05:33.520
like life is awesome.

00:05:33.520 --> 00:05:35.714
- Literally after this,
you're about to get on stage.

00:05:35.714 --> 00:05:37.078
- [Amber] Yeah.

00:05:37.078 --> 00:05:39.121
- What doe it feel like to
perform in front of hundreds

00:05:39.121 --> 00:05:40.417
of thousands of people?

00:05:40.417 --> 00:05:42.415
- It's still really something
I can't really fathom

00:05:42.415 --> 00:05:43.824
at the moment, you know, you're going from

00:05:43.824 --> 00:05:46.978
getting ready, and news
interviews, fan greets,

00:05:46.978 --> 00:05:48.266
and then you go and do the show,

00:05:48.266 --> 00:05:49.553
it just feels like a euphoric,

00:05:49.553 --> 00:05:50.875
like you see the fans
and they're all smiling

00:05:50.875 --> 00:05:52.197
and singing with you.

00:05:52.197 --> 00:05:54.214
- They allow you the
opportunity to do what you do.

00:05:54.214 --> 00:05:55.776
- Even if you meet just one fan,

00:05:55.776 --> 00:05:57.424
each experience is extremely humbling.

00:05:57.424 --> 00:05:59.503
I've been doing this for
seven, eight years now.

00:05:59.503 --> 00:06:01.738
It's awesome, but how do
I respond to all this?

00:06:01.738 --> 00:06:04.624
Someone like me, in my
position, you can definitely

00:06:04.624 --> 00:06:06.862
get big-headed really easily
and forget a lot of things

00:06:06.862 --> 00:06:08.445
to be thankful for.

00:06:08.445 --> 00:06:10.220
Every moment is precious,
and there's no time to hate

00:06:10.220 --> 00:06:14.067
or judge people, it's
just like "You're cool.

00:06:14.067 --> 00:06:15.639
Let's do something cool."

00:06:15.639 --> 00:06:17.256
- Every fan's dream right there.

00:06:17.256 --> 00:06:20.725
To hear that they're cool from
their favorite K-pop star.

00:06:20.725 --> 00:06:22.577
(cheering)

00:06:22.577 --> 00:06:25.160
(upbeat music)

00:06:36.520 --> 00:06:39.921
- Oh my gosh, you were so good.

00:06:39.921 --> 00:06:42.860
You were like "What's up
LA", everybody's like ah!

00:06:42.860 --> 00:06:45.683
You're like (mumbles) and their like ah!

00:06:45.683 --> 00:06:46.916
I still have the producer's schedule,

00:06:46.916 --> 00:06:51.083
now I'm going to film, so
life of a K-pop star, yeah!

00:06:51.978 --> 00:06:54.779
- Congratulations,
performing in your home town.

00:06:54.779 --> 00:06:56.074
- Thank you, and thank you for coming!

00:06:56.074 --> 00:06:56.907
- You're welcome.

00:06:56.907 --> 00:07:00.846
- Oh come on for more
hugs, hug, y'all have funs.

00:07:00.846 --> 00:07:03.179
(cheering)

